{
 "id": "098-kuslarin-sabah-konseri",
 "lang": "en",
 "title": "The Birds' Evening Concert",
 "theme": "Listening to the sounds of nature",
 "blurb": "One evening, Elif wants to listen to the forest's concert; but when she shouts with excitement, the sparrows fly away. Taking a deep breath and closing her eyes, Elif listens to the sparrows going to sleep, the owl waking up, and the song of silence.",
 "voiceNames": {
  "elif": "Elif",
  "nine": "Grandma",
  "serce": "The sparrows",
  "vrak": "Croak (frog)",
  "hubu": "Hoot (owl)",
  "kirpi": "Hedgehog"
 },
 "pages": [
  {
   "text": "It was evening. The sun was sinking behind the trees. Elif and her grandma were by the forest. Grandma smiled: “The forest's evening concert starts soon.” Elif's eyes lit up. “A concert? Where are the instruments?”",
   "hits": {
    "elif": {
     "say": "A concert? Where are the instruments?"
    },
    "nine": {
     "say": "Open your ears, you'll hear it soon."
    },
    "k": {
     "say": "Cheep cheep!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Grandma!",
   "ask": "Which instruments do you think are in the forest's concert? Which sounds do we hear?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Elif was so excited. She spun her wheels fast, fast, and rolled towards the birds. “HELLO, BIIIRDS!” she shouted. Flutter, flutter, flap! The sparrows took off and flew away. The forest went quiet as quiet. Elif's shoulders drooped. “Did I miss the concert?”",
   "hits": {
    "elif": {
     "say": "Did I miss the concert?"
    },
    "k": {
     "say": "Cheep! Too loud!"
    },
    "nine": {
     "say": "The birds got a fright, Elif dear."
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch the sparrows!",
   "ask": "Why did the sparrows fly away? How do you feel when you hear a very loud sound?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Grandma leaned beside her: “Loud sounds frighten birds. When evening comes, they look for a place to sleep.” Elif thought for a moment. Then she took a deep breath. Her chest rose slowly, fell slowly.",
   "hits": {
    "elif": {
     "say": "Breathe in… breathe out…"
    },
    "nine": {
     "say": "Loud sounds frighten birds."
    }
   },
   "predict": {
    "q": "What do you think Elif will do now?",
    "res": "Both are lovely, quiet ideas! Let's find out.",
    "opts": [
     {
      "l": "Closes her eyes and listens"
     },
     {
      "l": "Waits without moving"
     }
    ]
   },
   "hint": "Breathe with Elif!",
   "ask": "Let's take a deep breath like Elif. What happens in your body when you breathe in?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Elif had an idea: “If I close my eyes, my ears will hear better!” She closed her eyes. She listened hard, ever so carefully. At first there was no sound. Then… Cheep cheep cheep! From inside the bush. Croak croak! From the foot of the log. Rustle rustle! From among the dry leaves. Elif whispered: “The concert has started!”",
   "hits": {
    "serce": {
     "say": "Cheep cheep cheep!"
    },
    "vrak": {
     "say": "Croak croak!"
    },
    "kirpi": {
     "say": "Rustle rustle! It's me, the hedgehog!"
    },
    "elif": {
     "say": "The concert has started!"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Cheep, croak, rustle! You found who made all three sounds.",
    "msg": "You found them all!"
   },
   "hint": "Find who's making the sound!",
   "ask": "Close your eyes and listen. What sounds can you hear right now?",
   "cues": [
